**Security notes:**
- The client never receives the Algolia search API key; all searches go through a server-side proxy endpoint (`/api/search`) that authenticates, rate-limits, validates, and then calls Algolia.
- The `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALGOLIA_*` variables are only used for display purposes (app ID and index name) and never contain credentials.
- All user input is validated with Zod schemas before use.
- Highlighted HTML from Algolia is sanitized with an allowlist-based sanitizer before rendering.
- URLs are validated to ensure only `http:` and `https:` protocols are allowed.
- The server endpoint enforces authentication, rate limiting, and index name allowlisting.
